### Component 1: Injector (`injector/`)

The standalone Windows application that maps our DLL into WoW's process.

#### [NEW] [main.cpp](file:///Users/vardanvanyan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/wow-injection-bot/injector/src/main.cpp)
- Find WoW process by name (`Wow.exe`)
- Open process handle with `PROCESS_ALL_ACCESS`
- Call manual mapper to inject `core.dll`

#### [NEW] [manual_map.h](file:///Users/vardanvanyan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/wow-injection-bot/injector/src/manual_map.h) / [manual_map.cpp](file:///Users/vardanvanyan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/wow-injection-bot/injector/src/manual_map.cpp)
- **Why manual mapping?** `LoadLibrary` injection is trivially detected by Warden. Manual mapping:
  - Reads the DLL file from disk
  - Allocates memory in target process via `VirtualAllocEx`
  - Maps PE sections (headers, .text, .data, .rdata, etc.)
  - Resolves imports (walks IAT, resolves function addresses)
  - Processes relocations (fixes base address delta)
  - Executes TLS callbacks
  - Calls `DllMain` via `CreateRemoteThread` pointing to mapped entry
  - Erases PE headers from mapped memory (anti-forensics)
- Result: Our DLL exists in WoW's memory without appearing in the module list

